Grove PATCH-38: market-maker console for the Grove coins (price tiles, AMM script, identity copy)

Found 2026-09-17 reviewing the console as a maker would use it for ZEPH/ZANO.
Pwnda's own UI is taker-only, so makers create offers and run the AMM from
this console.

WHAT WAS WRONG

1. No ZANO or ZEPH price tile on the offers page. offers.html lists both with
   'show': false. Upstream hid Zano in bcd251c4 (2024-10), before upstream had
   any Zano chain support; PATCH-26 copied that flag for Zephyr. The data path
   is already there: offers-pricechart.js iterates CoinManager's coins (both
   registered by PATCH-26), its container list names 'zano' and 'zeph', and
   /json/coinprices, /json/coinvolume and /json/coinhistory resolve both
   tickers (ZEPH through PATCH-28's CoinGecko id, zephyr-protocol). Clicking a
   tile switches the chart through the same generic handler every coin uses.

2. The AMM could not start on Grove. ui/page_amm.py runs
   <datadir>/basicswap/scripts/createoffers.py, a file that lives in
   upstream's repository outside the Python package and is placed there only
   by upstream's own installers. A Grove datadir has no basicswap/ directory,
   so "Start" launched the interpreter on a missing file. The script itself is
   coin-generic: it resolves coins from /json/coins, defaults to adaptor_sig,
   and prices through /json/rates, so ZEPH and ZANO templates work unchanged.

   The script now ships inside the package as basicswap/scripts/createoffers.py,
   a verbatim copy of the pinned tag's scripts/createoffers.py carried as an
   applier asset (upstream/patches/assets/). The bundled copy is preferred
   because it is pinned to this engine's API (the ephemeral token the GUI
   passes); the datadir path stays as the fallback. Refresh the asset on every
   pin move: scripts/ammScriptAsset.test.mjs fails when it differs from the
   pinned clone.

3. The offer form described the "Send-from address" as "the address that will
   hold and lock the coins you send during the swap", and the new-address hint
   said it would "receive its locked funds". Both are false. addr_from goes to
   prepareSMSGAddress(): it is the Particl messaging identity the offer is
   announced from. Each swap locks funds in its own swap-derived addresses.
   A maker reading the old text could think funds sit in that address.

WHAT IS NOT CHANGED

The duplicate-process check in page_amm.py runs `ps aux`, which does not
exist on Windows; the exception is caught and the check returns no processes,
so only duplicate detection is lost there. Not patched.

Applies to: basicswap v0.18.9 (5471e609b9fbcba1a528dac60e2e06fc2f1a8ca4), after PATCH-37.
Marker: PWNDA-PATCH-38

